RAG for Research and Document Analysis:

This RAG system is built using LangGraph. 
Is purpose is to accurately extract and summarize text-based information retrieved from a library of pdfs, epub, txt, md, jpeg/jpg, png format documents.
During development, the model used for retrieval of documents and generation of responses was qwen3.8; the model used for grading and evaluation was a lighter-weight ption qwen2.5; for embeddings the nomic-embedding-model was used.
The workflow begins at ingestion of documents which loads the documents based on their type. After documents are loaded, they are vetorized into a ChromaDB vector database.
After ingestion the user can query a single question. The user can also start a chat. 
There is a checkpointer database for keeping track of a specific chat's history (a chat is associated with a thread-id), this enables the model to contextualize future responses.
There is also an in-memory cache so that the model does not have to retrieve the same documents again for a new query if what was previously retrieved contains relevant information.
The RAG is enhanced with concurrent grading which lowers the latency of the pipeline after the documents are retrieved. Concurrent grading of documents is achieved using LangGraph’s Send API - fan-out/map-reduce pattern.
Grading tasks run in parallel and then their updates are merged into a documents list which is then used to generate the answer.
The generation and evaluation rely on tailored prompts. Generation uses a prompt which instructs the generator model to answer the query with at least three pieces of evidence from texts retrieved.
Evaluation uses relevence and support prompts to instruct the evaluator model to decide on a scale from 0.0 to 1.0 how relevant each retrieved source is.

How To Use:
 
cd Rag-for-Research-Analysis-Agent

docker service start

docker compose build rag

To run ingestion:
docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest // To ingest everything in library 
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest --rebuild-index // To clear the vector database first then re-ingest all documents in the library
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.main ingest --file "/documents/determined - robert sapolsky.pdf" // To ingest one specific document from the library 

To check the vector database:
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m app.check_index // returns list of indexed documents, tool to check if ingestion an properly

To start querying:
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python app.main chat --thread-id test --clear-cache --clear-thread
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python app.main chat --thread-id test // After execution of that command, docker runs and a chat appears with a promp for a query
To exit chat print exit or quit
you> what is determinism in context of biology?
or
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python app.main ask --thread-id test --clear-cache --clear-thread "[Question]" // Or run a standalone question query

To run tests:
sudo docker compose run --rm  rag python -m tests.test_ingest
or 
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m tests.test_retrieval
or 
sudo docker compose run --rm rag python -m tests.test_graph

